---
source: text/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"bits\")"
---
Convert bit masks from/to various formats.

Each positional argument is a "group" of bits in one of the recognised input formats (hex `0x...`,
grouped hex `,xxxxxxxx,...`, or list `1,3,5-10`). Groups are combined left-to-right, OR'ing by
default; a leading `&`, `^`, or `~` selects AND, XOR, or ANDN instead. With no positional arguments,
groups are read from stdin one per line.

Usage: bits [OPTIONS] [MASKS]...

Arguments:
  [MASKS]...
          Mask or list groups (read from stdin if none given)

Options:
  -m, --mask
          Print result as a hexadecimal mask (default)

  -g, --grouped-mask
          Print result as 32-bit comma-separated hex groups

  -b, --binary
          Print result as a binary mask

  -l, --list
          Print result as a list of bit IDs (with ranges)

  -w, --width <WIDTH>
          Maximum number of bits handled; bits above this are truncated
          
          [default: 8192]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
